// Bitcoin Script Example: Bitwise Operations
//
// Transaction version: 2
// It keeps every intermediate value on the stack to show the steps, and
// version 1 requires exactly one item at the end.
//
// Demonstrates bitwise logic opcodes.
// These operate on bytes, not on JavaScript-style 32-bit integers,
// so they take and return byte strings. and/or/xor need operands of
// equal length.

// AND operation
// Bytewise: 0x0c & 0x0a = 0x08
12 10 and
// Stack: [0x08]

// OR operation
// Bytewise: 0x0c | 0x0a = 0x0e
12 10 or
// Stack: [0x08, 0x0e]

// XOR operation
// Bytewise: 0x0c ^ 0x0a = 0x06
12 10 xor
// Stack: [0x08, 0x0e, 0x06]

// Left shift
// Bitwise over the bytes: 0x05 << 2 = 0x14
5 2 lShift
// Stack: [0x08, 0x0e, 0x06, 0x14]

// Right shift
// Bitwise over the bytes: 0x14 >> 2 = 0x05
20 2 rShift
// Stack: [0x08, 0x0e, 0x06, 0x14, 0x05]

// Invert (bitwise NOT)
// Bytewise complement: ~0x05 = 0xfa
5 invert
// Stack: [0x08, 0x0e, 0x06, 0x14, 0x05, 0xfa]
